(6464837, 958962, 112575, '<td valign="top">In answer to Aarthek - Kolmanskop is a ghost town near Luderitz in Namibia. A small diamond mining community in what is still a very rich diamond area. Only has 20 or so buildings that are now a museum. The Namib desert has "invaded" some of the houses. An amazing place to spend a few hours with a camera - especially as it was "off season" when I was there. More on my blog at <a href="//coffeecools.wordpress.com/2011/06/26/kolmanskop-namibia-june-%e2%80%9811/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//coffeecools.wordpress.com/2011/06/26/kolmanskop-namibia-june-%e2%80%9811/</a></td>', 'In answer to Aarthek - Kolmanskop is a ghost town near Luderitz in Namibia. A small diamond mining community in what is still a very rich diamond area. Only has 20 or so buildings that are now a museum. The Namib desert has "invaded" some of the houses. An amazing place to spend a few hours with a camera - especially as it was "off season" when I was there. More on my blog at //coffeecools.wordpress.com/2011/06/26/kolmanskop-namibia-june-%e2%80%9811/', '2011-07-08 01:43:28.000000', NULL, 0),
