(6466581, 957076, 47470, '<td valign="top">Underrated, in my opinion, but I''m not so sure about your title.  That water looks much too choppy to be paradise : )  ...unless you mean a paradise for photographers!</td>', 'Underrated, in my opinion, but I''m not so sure about your title.  That water looks much too choppy to be paradise : )  ...unless you mean a paradise for photographers!', '2011-07-09 22:18:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6466673, 959723, 93565, '<td valign="top">I went ahead, out of curiosity, and copied a version into PS and did some BW messing around, and it turns out some interesting results, but they are a totally different feel from what you got here. They look almost abstract, and are a giant departure from the obvious scene we have here. I''m not really sure if I prefer it one way or the other, since it really depends what sort of a feeling you wanted to cast as to which is "better."<br/>Here''s what I mean...<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=961271" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/90000-94999/93565/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_961271.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/90000-94999/93565/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_961271.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/90000-94999/93565/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_961271.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>In any case, emphasizing the contrast a bit might have helped this, and differentiated the posts from the water.</td>', 'I went ahead, out of curiosity, and copied a version into PS and did some BW messing around, and it turns out some interesting results, but they are a totally different feel from what you got here. They look almost abstract, and are a giant departure from the obvious scene we have here. I''m not really sure if I prefer it one way or the other, since it really depends what sort of a feeling you wanted to cast as to which is "better."Here''s what I mean...  In any case, emphasizing the contrast a bit might have helped this, and differentiated the posts from the water.', '2011-07-10 04:22:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(6466674, 959743, 93565, '<td valign="top">You certainly got some good comments for this one, Joe. You''ve got a penchant for entering photos that push the boundaries, and they rarely fail to make me laugh.</td>', 'You certainly got some good comments for this one, Joe. You''ve got a penchant for entering photos that push the boundaries, and they rarely fail to make me laugh.', '2011-07-10 04:34:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(6466676, 959840, 93565, '<td valign="top">You won our friendly competition, and rightfully so. This really is a nice one, I love the crisp detail, as it makes the softness of the fuzz all the more palpable.</td>', 'You won our friendly competition, and rightfully so. This really is a nice one, I love the crisp detail, as it makes the softness of the fuzz all the more palpable.', '2011-07-10 04:39:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6466681, 959745, 93565, '<td valign="top">A scion sunset.<br/>I''ve always liked brooding photos, and this one is no different. The drab scene just makes the color all the more remarkable, and I really enjoy that. The clouds/fog also help to close the scene in; very nice.</td>', 'A scion sunset.I''ve always liked brooding photos, and this one is no different. The drab scene just makes the color all the more remarkable, and I really enjoy that. The clouds/fog also help to close the scene in; very nice.', '2011-07-10 04:44:20.000000', NULL, 0),
